node_definition.done_when:
Make the continuous fast map's diverted solve converge to 1e-12 at 550 and 2,098 cells, as it now does at 282. Lead rulings: the batched per-state H200 wall is the target (0.90 ms), and the limited-to-diverted transition is continuous, with both boundary candidates computed every step and no discrete verdict in the iteration.

Where it stands (on main, docs/research/fast-map-production.html, prototype scripts/prototypes/fast_map_production, merged at b47f4c3a4):
- The map is continuous. The wall candidate is a path strength, the containing cell owns the X-point booking, and a local sector replaces the distant-axis lookup. Fine-step and two random-direction scans show maximum adjacent residual changes of 4.6e-10 and 1.3e-9.
- Analytic map error is 1.09e-3, 4.9e-4 and 8.7e-5 at 282, 550 and 2,098 cells.
- At 282 cells the diverted solve converges:
  - the cold solve reaches 1.25e-13 in five corrections;
  - the gradient is 1.5e-11 at the solution, and Taylor slopes are 2.00 along three directions;
  - warm two-correction solves reach 1e-13;
  - the width-128 chord batch converges 128/128 at 0.309 ms per state.
- At 550 and 2,098 cells the diverted solve stops at 1.550e-3 and 3.627e-3.
  - At 550 the Gauss-Newton gradient ratio is 0.586, so the iterate is not a residual minimum.
  - A 401-point scan along the Newton direction is smooth, with support fixed at 337 cells, but reaches only 1.55026e-3 at step 1.5e-4 from 1.55037e-3.
  - Backtracking accepts factors down to 1.9e-6 and still stops.
  - A two-norm merit decreases by only 1.7e-10.
- At 2,098, owner cell 47 has normal-form membership 0.0285 against ordinary fraction 0.460. The previous node did not measure cell-by-cell agreement at the normal-form/ordinary-cut handoff.
- The earlier moment-space Newton also recorded JVP disagreement on the 2,098-cell diverted and 5,167-cell limited carriers.

Done when docs/research/fine-grid-convergence.html (reckon-type research, plan-informs converged-forward-solve) reports these H200 measurements on the diverted carriers at about 550 and 2,098 cells:

(1) Whether the Jacobian matches the map at the stalled iterates.
- Run a Taylor remainder test along the Newton direction and three random directions, over 1e-2 to 1e-8, per moment block. Locate any block or cell whose remainder is first order (a kink), or does not shrink (a wrong derivative).
- Report the handoff cells: four-crossing cells inside and next to the X-point region. For each, give its normal-form and ordinary-cut membership and moments, and their one-sided derivatives.

(2) The cause, named at a cell and a term. For example:
- a membership or moment that is continuous but not differentiable at the normal-form/ordinary handoff;
- a JVP that differentiates a stop_gradient, clip or where branch inconsistently with the primal;
- a sector or path-strength weight with a derivative kink;
- or a genuine absence of a nearby root.

(3) A fix at that mechanism. It must keep the map continuous, keep analytic map error falling with resolution, and add no topology branch and no widened tolerance. Then show:
- the diverted cold solve reaching 1e-12 at 550 and 2,098, plus 282, with residual histories;
- the Gauss-Newton gradient at each solution;
- Taylor slopes of 2 at each solution;
- warm two-correction neighbours;
- the runtime-argument two-correction chord batch (the scripts/prototypes/batched_factor structure) at widths 1, 16 and 128, with converged counts and per-state wall against 0.90 ms;
- cold compile and executable size against 60 s and 50 MB.

(4) The limited carriers at the same sizes and the 41-state sweep validity at 282 and 550, unchanged. Transition continuity to roundoff across a bisected bracket at 550.

(5) Figures under docs/figures/converged-forward-solve/fine-grid-convergence, following AGENTS.md plotting rules: Taylor slopes per block and resolution, residual histories, and one poloidal line-contour panel per terminal forward state. Each panel shows solved and analytic flux on shared levels, both null sets and the wall, with no axes, and the terminal residual and converged flag in the caption.

Negative controls must re-run the program rather than read a frozen receipt:
- reverting the fix reproduces the 550-cell stall at about 1.55e-3, so its row turns red;
- a Jacobian with the identified term perturbed fails the Taylor slope test.

Write only scripts/prototypes/fine_grid_convergence, docs/research/fine-grid-convergence.html, docs/figures/converged-forward-solve/fine-grid-convergence and docs/evidence/fragments/converged-forward-solve/fine-grid-convergence.html, with plan-evidence-for converged-forward-solve. Import, but do not edit, scripts/prototypes/{fast_map_production,batched_factor,fused_convergence,fast_read,lean_map,diverted_stall} and nova/. Carry a corrected copy of any imported function under your own path and name the function it replaces. Do not change nova/ product code, and do not touch the held moment-space Newton worktree. reckon audit-doc must report 0 errors.

Run conditions: H200 rows run as one job through RECKON_ALLOW_NESTED_LAUNCH=1 scripts/h200_test_lane/run.sh --log (an absolute path in the run directory) --wait -- (targets), or one sbatch job on --partition=betelgeuse --reservation=gpu_0003_grpA --gres=gpu:1 with rungs as rows inside the allocation (never an array), --time sized to finish, XLA_PYTHON_CLIENT_PREALLOCATE=false and TMPDIR=/tmp in the submit environment and in every child; submit for real and read squeue a minute later rather than trusting sbatch --test-only. On a compute node run /home/ITER/mcintos/Code/nova/.venv/bin/python directly with PYTHONPATH set to the run worktree and never invoke uv; every login-node uv command carries --no-sync and nothing runs uv sync. configure_dtypes() before any array and jax_enable_x64 asserted True. Gates pass by delta against orientation_base_sha in per-module fresh processes, both arms running the same test files with the repository root conftest, baseline_suite and after_suite as single-line JSON whose log_path names one log file and whose command is literally runnable. Any wait is declared on the job that finishes last as wait_probe ["sacct","-n","-X","-P","-j","(job id)","-o","State"] and wait_terminal ["COMPLETED","FAILED","CANCELLED","TIMEOUT","OUT_OF_MEMORY","NODE_FAIL"] as JSON lists, and names every job it depends on in wait_condition. The certified 550, 2,000 and 5,000-cell machines and exteriors are cached under /home/ITER/mcintos/.config/reckon/crew/runs/r-20261009T181553786165-proto-support/ordered/rows/cache and may be read in place, never written. Run filepath relativize over any evidence fragment before committing. Commit with conventional subjects and bodies at every step and write the manifest and commit before every job wait; the manifest commits line lists every commit; status is complete, blocked or failed, which the worker sets itself. No plan labels in source names or comments. Inside every job payload, make one directory with mktemp -d /tmp/$USER-$SLURM_JOB_ID-XXXX, point TMPDIR at it, and remove it on exit with trap 'rm -rf' (keep TMPDIR=/tmp in the submit environment so slurmstepd can start). Never leave extracted base trees or caches in /tmp after a node ends; anything a later reader needs goes under the run directory on GPFS.

Import provenance: print nova.__file__ in every log header. On the fleet allocation (SLURM_JOB_ID set), run CPU work in place. The time budget is per working turn, not a deadline: park on H200 jobs with declared waits and continue across turns; this node is sized at about 8 worker-hours, and an unmeasured item in your own scope is remaining work, not a blocker. Never edit a script a submitted job will run; submit a per-job copy. Size every job memory from a measured row. The manifest commits line lists every commit (git rev-list), orientation_base_sha is copied from git rev-parse output, and status is complete when the record is delivered even if the target is not met (then give the nearest measured figure and what dominates it).

